@startuml Radar_Ingestion_SysML
' ============================================================
' SysML Activity Diagram: Marine Radar Ingestion + Hybrid Navy
' Source: merchantnavydecoded.com – Marine Radar Complete Guide
' ============================================================

skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam activityBackgroundColor #E8F4FD
skinparam activityBorderColor #2E86AB
skinparam activityBorderThickness 1.5
skinparam activityFontColor #1A1A2E
skinparam activityFontSize 12
skinparam activityDiamondBackgroundColor #FFF3CD
skinparam activityDiamondBorderColor #E6A817
skinparam activityDiamondFontColor #1A1A2E
skinparam arrowColor #2E86AB
skinparam arrowThickness 1.5
skinparam swimlaneBorderColor #6C757D
skinparam swimlaneBorderThickness 2
skinparam swimlaneBackgroundColor #F8F9FA
skinparam swimlaneFontSize 13
skinparam swimlaneFontStyle bold
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFFDE7
skinparam noteBorderColor #F0A500

title <b>SysML Activity Diagram – Marine Radar Ingestion & Hybrid Navy Parallel Flow</b>\n<i>Source: Merchant Navy Decoded – The Complete Guide About Marine Radar</i>

' ── SWIM LANES ─────────────────────────────────────────────
|#DCEEFB|Transmitter Layer|
|#E8F5E9|Scanner / Aerial Layer|
|#FBE9E7|Receiver / Signal Processing Layer|
|#EDE7F6|Display & Plotting Layer|
|#E0F7FA|Hybrid Navy Integration Layer|

' ============================================================
' SECTION 1 – TRANSMITTER
' ============================================================
|Transmitter Layer|

start

:Power Supply Initialization;

note right
  Provides regulated DC power
  to all transmitter sub-units
end note

:Delay Line & Trigger Generation;
:Modulator Activation;

note right
  Modulator shapes the pulse
  width and timing envelope
end note

:Magnetron → High-Frequency RF Oscillation;

' ── X-Band vs S-Band Fork ──────────────────────────────────
fork
  :<<X-Band>>\n9 GHz / 3 cm wavelength\nHigh resolution, short range\nBetter target discrimination\nSmaller antenna – suits small vessels;
fork again
  :<<S-Band>>\n3 GHz / 10 cm wavelength\nLong range detection\nWeather-resistant (rain/fog)\nRequired for ships >3000 GT (SOLAS);
end fork

:TR Switch → Transmit Mode\n(Waveguide / Coaxial Cable Routing);

' ============================================================
' SECTION 2 – SCANNER / AERIAL
' ============================================================
|Scanner / Aerial Layer|

:Scanner Located on Monkey Island\n(Clear of all obstructions);
:Unidirectional Beam Emission\n@ Pulse Repetition Frequency (PRF): 500–4000 pps;

note right
  Scanner rotates 12–30 RPM
  clockwise when viewed from above.
  One trace per pulse transmitted.
end note

:Rotational Scan – 360° Coverage;
:Echo Reception from Targets;
:TR Switch → Receive Mode;

' ============================================================
' SECTION 3 – RECEIVER / SIGNAL PROCESSING
' ============================================================
|Receiver / Signal Processing Layer|

:TR Cell (Transmitter-Receiver Switch)\nProtects receiver during transmission;
:Local Oscillator + Mixer\n(Downconvert to Intermediate Frequency);
:IF Amplifier\n(Amplify weak echo signals);
:Video Amplifier;
:Demodulator\n(Smooth & condition the signal);

' ── Range & Bearing Fork ───────────────────────────────────
fork
  :Range Determination\nRange Rings & Variable Range Markers (VRM)\nAccuracy: ±30 m or 1% of range scale;
  note right
    Tracing spot speed = ½ speed of radio waves.
    Echo returns to same spot as the trace,
    brightening it to indicate target range.
  end note
fork again
  :Bearing Determination\nHeading Marker + Bearing Scale\nAccuracy: ±1°;
  note right
    PRF (500–4000) >> RPM (12–30) so
    angle rotated between TX & RX echo
    is negligible – bearing is accurate.
  end note
end fork

' ============================================================
' SECTION 4 – DISPLAY & PLOTTING
' ============================================================
|Display & Plotting Layer|

:PPI Display (CRT – Cathode Ray Tube)\nPlan Position Indicator – Bird's Eye View;

note right
  Electron beam sweeps radially
  from center to edge, synchronized
  with scanner rotation.
end note

:Target Paint – Bright Spot on Screen;
:Bearing Scale (numbered every 30°, marked every 5°)\nMinimum 4 Parallel Index Lines;

' ── SOLAS ARPA Decision ────────────────────────────────────
if (Ship Tonnage?) then (> 3000 GT)
  :ARPA – Automatic Radar Plotting Aid\n(Mandatory – SOLAS Chapter V);
  :CPA / TCPA Calculation\n(Closest Point of Approach / Time to CPA);
  :Automatic Target Acquisition & Tracking;
else (300–3000 GT)
  :Electronic Plotting Aid (EPA)\n(Mandatory – SOLAS Chapter V);
  :Semi-Automated Target Tracking;
endif

' ── Sensor Failure Alarm ───────────────────────────────────
if (Signal / Sensor Failure?) then (Yes – Gyro / Log / Video / Sync / Heading)
  :ALARM – Failure Indication Triggered\n(IMO Resolution MSC.192(79));
  :Standby Mode\n(Radar resumes within 5 sec from Standby\nor within 4 min from Cold Start);
else (No)
  :System Operating at Optimum Performance\n(Absence-of-Target Indication Active);
endif

' ============================================================
' SECTION 5 – PARALLEL FORK: STANDARD vs HYBRID NAVY
' ============================================================

fork
  ' ── Standard Radar Output ──────────────────────────────
  |Display & Plotting Layer|
  :Standard Radar Collision Avoidance Output\n(Officer of the Watch Assessment);
  :Navigation Decision & Course Adjustment;

fork again
  ' ── Hybrid Navy Parallel Flow ──────────────────────────
  |Hybrid Navy Integration Layer|

  :AIS Data Ingestion\n(Vessel ID, MMSI, Position, COG, SOG, Heading);

  note right
    AIS = Automatic Identification System.
    Complements radar with vessel identity
    not available from echo alone.
  end note

  fork
    :Satellite Data Feed\n(VDES / GNSS Augmentation\nPosition Accuracy Enhancement);
  fork again
    :ECDIS Chart Overlay\n(Electronic Navigational Chart – ENC\nReal-time chart integration);
  fork again
    :Drone / UAV Sensor Feed\n(Extended Beyond-Horizon\nSituational Awareness);
  end fork

  :AI / ML Target Classification Engine\n(Vessel Type · Threat Level · Behaviour Anomaly);

  note right
    Fuses radar echo geometry with
    AIS metadata, AIS gap detection,
    and historical movement patterns.
  end note

  :Sensor Fusion Engine\n(Radar + AIS + Satellite + ECDIS + UAV → Unified Track);
  :Integrated Bridge System (IBS)\n(Unified Operational Picture for OOW);
  :Hybrid Collision Avoidance Decision Support\n(COLREGS-aware Recommendation Engine);

end fork

' ============================================================
' FINAL OUTPUT
' ============================================================
|Display & Plotting Layer|

:Navigation & Safety Output\n(Course Recommendation · Alert · Logging);

stop

@enduml
